ncentración de contratos al límite no refleja actos maliciosos. Puede deberse a necesidades específicas o a precios de mercado. No implica que se haya sobrepasado el límite ni que se haya actuado de forma irregular.\nQué se puede revisar: Comprobar si los contratos [1], [2], [3] atienden la misma necesidad. Verificar si el adjudicatario A repite contratos en otros ámbitos. Analizar si los contratos al límite se distribuyen uniformemente entre los adjudicatarios.","en":"What the data shows: Between 2023 and 2025, this body awarded 66 minor contracts for services and supplies above 14,000 and up to 15,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 18.8 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 3.5, with a 95% confidence interval of 2.5 to 4.9. December accounts for 12% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 10% of all its services and supplies contracts. The awardee with the most contracts just under the limit, called awardee A here, has 5. Contract [1], for 14,700 euros, was awarded in December 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The concentration of contracts in December and the high number of unique awardees do not prove improper actions. Statistical trends alone do not indicate wrongdoing, as market conditions or budget constraints could explain the data.\nWhat can be checked: Check the distribution of contracts across December and verify if multiple contracts served the same need. Review awardee A's contracts to see if they align with their stated services or if there's repetition of similar orders.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["jLDop0rVx4Z%2BF6L2uCfUWg%3D%3D","4suey64tIAQ4NavIWzMcHA%3D%3D","vHVWV%2BD3nXJ9Zh%2FyRJgM8w%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-16"}}